[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2489926049","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99438#issuecomment-2489926049","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99438","id":2489926049,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6UaUGh","user":{"login":"reach-satori","id":30383615,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzgzNjE1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30383615?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/reach-satori","html_url":"https://github.com/reach-satori","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reach-satori/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reach-satori/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reach-satori/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reach-satori/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reach-satori/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reach-satori/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reach-satori/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reach-satori/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/reach-satori/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-21T02:16:17Z","updated_at":"2024-11-21T02:24:26Z","body":"Looks like the inner popup window steals focus. Same happens with MenuButton because it also has a popup. Although I'm getting slightly different behaviour on item 4 there, on linux. Adding this to your mrp:\n```gdscript\n\t$\"OptionButton\".get_popup().focus_entered.connect(func_print.bind(\"popup entered\"))\n\t$\"OptionButton\".get_popup().focus_exited.connect(func_print.bind(\"popup exited\"))\n```\nthis is what I get\n```\nenter  # Startup\nexit  # Click outside, first exit, normal\nenter  # Click on the option button, main window gets focus, normal\nexit  # \"problem\" focus loss, happens immediately after previous enter, because of the popup\npopup entered  # popup window takes focus\n```\nNo second entry, different ordering.\n\nClicking *off* the option button afterward results in some more weird behaviour but I don't know if that's related.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2489926049/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2571715551","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99438#issuecomment-2571715551","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99438","id":2571715551,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZSUPf","user":{"login":"Klaim","id":142265,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MjI2NQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/142265?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Klaim","html_url":"https://github.com/Klaim","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Klaim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Klaim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Klaim/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Klaim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Klaim/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Klaim/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Klaim/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Klaim/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Klaim/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-05T18:40:36Z","updated_at":"2025-01-05T18:40:36Z","body":"For info, this affects any game that tries to pause the game when the window loses focus (detected through`get_window().focus_exited`) but also uses option-buttons in some UI (like my game which  uses 4.3-stable).\n\nWhen the `get_window().focus_exited` signal is sent, is there any way to workaround the issue by detecting if a subwindow has been focused?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2571715551/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]